<title>UK: SOCCER-COLLATED WORLD CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-COLLATED WORLD CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Collated results of World Cup,</p>
<p>European group qualifiers on Saturday:</p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p>In Chisinau: Moldova 1 Italy 3 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Moldova - Alexandru Curtianu (11th)</p>
<p>Italy - Fabrizio Ravanelli (8th, 87th), Pierluigi Casiraghi</p>
<p>(68th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 15,000</p>
<p>Group four</p>
<p>In Tallinn: Estonia 1 Belarus 1-0 (halftime 0-0)</p>
<p>Scorer: Sergei Hohlov-Simson (52nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 900</p>
<p>In Riga: Latvia 0 Scotland 2 (0-1)</p>
<p>Scorers: John Collins (18th), Darren Jackson (77th)</p>
<p>Attendance: 9,500</p>
<p>Group seven</p>
<p>In Cardiff: Wales 1 Netherlands 3 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Wales - Dean Saunders (17th)</p>
<p>Netherlands - Pierre Van Hooijdonk 2 (72nd, 75th), Ronald De</p>
<p>Boer (79th)</p>
<p>Group eight</p>
<p>In Vilnius: Lithuania 2 Iceland 0 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers: Edgars Jankauskas (penalty, 22nd), Vaidotas Shlekys</p>
<p>(73rd)</p>
<p>Attendance 4,000</p>
<p>Group nine</p>
<p>In Kiev: Ukraine 2 Portugal 1 (1-0)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Ukraine - Serhiy Popov (5th), Yuri Maksimov (88th)</p>
<p>Portugal - Luis Figo (83rd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 40,000</p>
<p>In Belfast: Northern Ireland 1 Armenia 1 (1-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Northern Ireland - Neil Lennon (30th)</p>
<p>Armenia - Eric Adouyan (8th)</p>
</text>
